title: Relay /health runs blocking git rev-parse subprocess per request when RAILWAY_GIT_COMMIT_SHA unset
updated_at: "2026-07-15T20:57:25Z"
---
ocaml/relay.ml handle_health (lines ~3313-3318): if RAILWAY_GIT_COMMIT_SHA is not set, the health handler falls back to Unix.open_process_in "git rev-parse --short HEAD" on EVERY /health request. In the Docker image .git is absent so it fails, but forking a subprocess synchronously inside the request handler is a latent slow-health / resource risk — and Railway health checks hit /health frequently. On prod the env var is normally set (fast path), so this is latent, not the current outage cause. Fix: resolve git_hash ONCE at startup (memoize) instead of per-request, and never fork in the hot request path. Priority low.